{"lines": ["Sometimes the problem is not the code. It is the story around it.", "The Beale ciphers. Three coded pages. One of them said to reveal where gold, silver and jewels were buried, estimated at more than sixty million dollars.", "The tale comes from a pamphlet published in 1885, called The Beale Papers. A man named Thomas Beale, around 1820, buried treasure in Bedford County, Virginia. He left a box with an innkeeper, Robert Morriss, and was never seen again.", "One of the three pages was solved. The second, which lists what was buried, uses the Declaration of Independence as its key. The first, the location, and the third, the owners, are unsolved.", "But in 1980, the cryptographer Jim Gillogly wrote an article called \"A Dissenting Opinion\". In 1982, Joe Nickell examined the pamphlet, found words such as \"stampeding\" that seem too modern, and doubted that Thomas Beale ever existed.", "No treasure has ever been found.", "Rule five. Before you decode the message, ask whether the story is the puzzle."], "words": [["Sometimes", 0.0, 0.42], ["the", 0.42, 0.84], ["problem", 0.84, 1.18], ["is", 1.18, 1.52], ["not", 1.52, 1.78], ["the", 1.78, 1.98], ["code.", 1.98, 2.28], ["It", 2.94, 3.02], ["is", 3.02, 3.12], ["the", 3.12, 3.28], ["story", 3.28, 3.7], ["around", 3.7, 4.02], ["it.", 4.02, 4.38], ["The", 5.2, 5.25], ["Beale", 5.25, 5.88], ["ciphers.", 5.88, 6.52], ["Three", 6.52, 6.84], ["coded", 6.84, 7.24], ["pages.", 7.24, 7.56], ["One", 8.46, 8.66], ["of", 8.66, 8.8], ["them", 8.8, 8.94], ["said", 8.94, 9.2], ["to", 9.2, 9.38], ["reveal", 9.38, 9.64], ["where", 9.64, 10.02], ["gold,", 10.02, 10.32], ["silver", 10.74, 10.98], ["and", 10.98, 11.36], ["jewels", 11.36, 11.6], ["were", 11.6, 11.94], ["buried,", 11.94, 12.36], ["estimated", 12.78, 13.14], ["at", 13.14, 13.66], ["more", 13.66, 13.88], ["than", 13.88, 14.1], ["sixty", 14.1, 14.46], ["million", 14.46, 14.88], ["dollars.", 14.88, 15.88], ["The", 15.88, 16.34], ["tale", 16.34, 16.54], ["comes", 16.54,